# ACDD Lint

**ACDD Lint** (`acdd lint` / `code_map_lint`) enforces architectural boundaries, documentation integrity, syntax health, and graph hygiene in one deterministic pass over `.acdd/code-map.sqlite`.

| Category | What it checks | Enabled in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **`arch`** | All 8 `ArchRuleKind` primitives from `.acdd/lint/*.yaml` (`lint_dirs:`) and Markdown `acdd-rule` blocks | Default (`verify`) & Full |
| **`docs`** | Frontmatter, broken Markdown links/anchors, unresolved symbol claims, stale symbol ranges, duplicate `INV-*`, orphan invariants, invalid `acdd-rule` YAML | Default (`verify`) & Full |
| **`syntax`** | Tree-sitter parse errors (`syntax.parse`), fact-budget caps, intra-crate type homonyms, and file-monolith ratchets (`max_file_prod_lines` / `max_file_prod_lines_error`) | Default (`verify`) & Full |
| **`duplicates`** | Asymmetric Probe-vs-Workspace AST statement clones (`>= 0.80` promoted to Error on newly introduced diff clones) + graph-ranked `0.45..0.80` `reuse_hints` | `tasks.build` & Full (`--categories all`) |
| **`dead_tails`** | Unreachable symbols (`dead_tails.unreachable`), phantom-tested helpers (`dead_tails.phantom_tested`), unresolved calls (`dead_tails.dangling_call`), and opt-in `dead_tails.unused_public_api` | Full (`--categories all`) |
| **`cycles`** | Strongly connected call and import cycles (`cycles.scc`) | Full (`--categories all`) |

Next: read **[Writing Docs, Linter Rules & Using `acdd lint`](/docs/lint/writing-docs-and-rules/)** for step-by-step instructions and complete rule examples.
